---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Factory & Quality Control"
  description="Manufacturing and quality-control approach for the Qinghe filter industry cluster, with production equipment and testing standards."
  breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Factory', href: '/factory/' }]}
>
  <main class="wrap" style="padding-top:2rem;">
    <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> / Factory</nav>
    <h1>Factory &amp; Quality Control</h1>

    <p class="lede">
      Manufacturing is positioned within the Qinghe filter industry cluster of Hebei province.
      Factory area, staffing and production equipment for this entity are marked provisional until
      independently verified with on-site evidence.
    </p>

    <h2>Production capability (industry reference)</h2>
    <p>
      Filter manufacturing in this cluster typically spans several dedicated lines — air-filter
      assembly, HEPA mini-pleat and separator pleating, filter-media production, and cleanroom
      equipment assembly. The following capability descriptions are drawn from the industry cluster
      reference corpus and are <em>not</em> presented as this entity's verified equipment list:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Filter media lines</strong> — needle-punched and synthetic-fibre media production with lamination.</li>
      <li><strong>HEPA pleating</strong> — separator and mini-pleat lines using micro-glass media (pleat depths 20–100 mm).</li>
      <li><strong>Frame forming</strong> — galvanised and stainless frame welding and forming.</li>
      <li><strong>Quality testing</strong> — efficiency, leakage and pressure-drop test equipment.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Quality control</h2>
    <p>
      Quality control follows a source-and-label discipline: every specification field carries a
      data-status label (<code>verified</code> / <code>catalog-confirmed</code> / <code>reference</code> /{' '}
      <code>pending</code>). HEPA elements are leak-tested before dispatch where a factory
      leakage-test certificate is specified. The{' '}
      <a href={`${site.dataSubsiteUrl}/reference/test-standards/`} rel="noopener" target="_blank">test-standards reference</a>{' '}
      documents the efficiency classifications applied across the range.
    </p>

    <h2>Certifications</h2>
    <p class="notice">
      Certifications are not presented until independently verified with certificate numbers. Any
      certification claim seen in third-party catalogues is not attributed to this entity.
    </p>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
